  "details": "1. Launched VRChat from Steam on Steam Audio Beta in PC mode. (Placed me in my home world)\n\n2. Launched world, but also clicked \"Invite Me\" beforehand from website.(https://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_d8857e5b-b5df-4906-ab1c-0982e2884710) \n\n3. Second VRC instance pops up with me in the world linked above. SteamVR Error pops up saying critical error has occured, so I just hit quit SteamVR but it did not boot me from the world or close VRChat, instead i was just able to move freely on desktop mode. (Join different worlds, talk to different people, etc.) avatar changing happened cross instances, so one avatar change in one world would affect the other.\n\nYou cannot join the same instance as yourself. (Same account detected in instance error) will boot you back to your home.\n\nPhotos / Video included of me in different worlds at the same time. Mic works as well. (where I briefly asked someone if my mic works)\n\nI am not invisible in either world, (people were interacting, I even got told to switch into a medium avatar, sorry club)\n\nLog files can be provided on request since I'm not sure if they have any personal info in them and I haven't scrubbed through, video (https://youtu.be/mm-Uh81B8W4) + photos attached.",
